#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:1
msgid "The income-tax year: four instalments and the annual Renta"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:3
msgid ""
"This page covers one full IRPF year for an example taxpayer: four "
"quarterly Modelo 130 instalments, each building on the ones before it, "
"closing with the annual Modelo 100 Renta declaration that gathers the "
"whole year. You start from an empty store; by the end you have prepared "
"and exported every IRPF filing the year asks of a self-employed "
"consultant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:9
msgid ""
"Cadrumo (the `aeat` command) prepares local files for Spanish tax forms. "
"It does not submit them to the Agencia Estatal de Administración "
"Tributaria (AEAT). At each filing you upload the exported file yourself "
"through the AEAT portal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:14
msgid ""
"Meet the persona this run-through follows: Ana García López, a consultant"
" (*consultoría*) who started her activity on January 1, 2026, invoices "
"her clients with 21 percent IVA, and buys office material as she goes. "
"The same persona and the same ledger continue in [The IVA year](iva-"
"lifecycle.md) - the two run-throughs describe the same business from two "
"tax angles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:21
msgid ""
"The CLI prints help, labels, and messages in Spanish. This page keeps the"
" explanations in English and quotes real Spanish output where it shows "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:24
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:26
msgid ""
"You need a working `aeat` command (see [Install Cadrumo](../workstation-"
"setup.md)) and a master-key passphrase. `aeat` encrypts your data with a "
"passphrase and prompts for it the first time each command runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:31
msgid "Stage 1: set up the taxpayer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:33
msgid ""
"Create the profile with `aeat config profile`, as [Set up your taxpayer "
"profile](profile-setup.md) walks through. The documentation sandbox "
"provisions its own profile, so this create is shown as a display frame:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:40
msgid ""
"The `--name` and `--surnames` are required: the export step refuses "
"without an operator name. The `--activity-start-date` marks when the "
"activity began, so `aeat` does not look for a filing from before your "
"first period. The sample `--tax-id` has the shape of a Spanish citizen's "
"NIF; use your own NIF, CIF, DNI, or NIE for a real profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:46
msgid "Confirm what the year will ask of Ana:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:52
msgid ""
"The calendar lists the four Modelo 130 windows (April, July, October, "
"January) and the annual Renta window the following spring. `explain` "
"shows why Modelo 130 applies: an activity under estimación directa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:56
msgid "Stage 2: the first quarter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:58
msgid ""
"Record the first quarter's activity - one sale, one expense. The "
"`--amount` is the gross total (taxable base plus IVA), and an expense row"
" needs a `--category-id` (list the valid ids with `aeat app ledger "
"categories`). The two `ledger add` commands appear as the collapsed setup"
" of the sequence below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:63
msgid ""
"Create and calculate the first instalment. Modelo 130 is cumulative, and "
"a true first period has no history, so the three prior-period carries are"
" passed as zeros - this is the only quarter where you do this. The "
"sequence below records the quarter's two rows, creates and calculates the"
" draft, and verifies it; the export, file, and reconcile commands that "
"close the quarter are shown after the verified result (they run against "
"your own evidenced, filed history, not the sandbox):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:75
msgid ""
"The key figures show the year so far: 1000 earned, 500 spent, and an "
"instalment of 20 percent on the net:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:84
msgid ""
"(The final result is 0.00 here because the minoración for low net income "
"absorbs the whole instalment - casilla 13 in the output shows it.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:87
msgid ""
"Verify reports `completeness_status complete` and "
"`granted_verificado_completo true` (the sequence above asserts this). "
"Export writes the fichero-BOE file and prints its path, size, and SHA-256"
" checksum - note the checksum; it identifies exactly which file you "
"upload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:92
msgid ""
"Upload the file at the AEAT portal (the checklist is [Upload your "
"exported modelo at the AEAT portal](file-at-aeat.md)), then record the "
"filing locally with `aeat app modelo work file` while the presentation "
"window is open. `work file` saves a local marker only - it does not "
"submit anything. The marker is what lets the next quarter's carries "
"resolve from this one. Finally, pull the justificante with `aeat app "
"modelo reconcile pull` so the official receipt is on record. All three "
"commands (export, file, reconcile pull) are shown after the verified "
"result in the sequence above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:101
msgid "Stage 3: the second and third quarters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:103
msgid ""
"The year continues; record each quarter's activity as it happens. For the"
" second quarter, say Ana invoices twice and buys once. Now the cumulative"
" behaviour shows itself: the second-quarter draft calculates with NO "
"`--binding` zeros, resolving the carries from the filed first quarter. "
"The whole second quarter runs against Ana's evidenced, filed first-"
"quarter record and inside the July presentation window, neither of which "
"the frozen documentation sandbox can reproduce, so the chain is shown as "
"display frames:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:114
msgid "Read the revision and compare it with the first quarter's:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:116
msgid ""
"Casilla `01` (ingresos) now covers January through June - the ledger "
"window for `2T` is the year to date, not the quarter alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:118
msgid ""
"Casilla `05` (pagos fraccionados anteriores) carries the instalment you "
"paid in the first quarter, read from your own filed record."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:120
msgid ""
"If an earlier quarter had ended negative, casilla `15` would offset it "
"here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:123
msgid ""
"If calculate blocks instead with a cross-period finding, the first "
"quarter is not filed and evidenced on your record - go back to stage 2 "
"and file and reconcile it. The tool never invents the missing quarter; a "
"visible blank beats a guessed zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:128
msgid ""
"The third quarter is the same chain one period later, with `3T` in place "
"of `2T` throughout. Every quarter after the first is this one rhythm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:131
msgid "Stage 4: the fourth quarter closes the instalment year"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:133
msgid ""
"Run the same chain for `4T` in January of the following year, the fourth "
"quarter's presentation window being January 1 to 30. After it is filed, "
"Ana has four instalments on record; together they are the payments on "
"account the annual declaration will set against her full-year income."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:138
msgid "Check the year's IRPF position at any point:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:144
msgid "Stage 5: the annual Renta declaration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:146
msgid ""
"The following spring, the annual Modelo 100 gathers the year. It is "
"annual, so the period token is `0A`, and the filing year is the income "
"year - the 2026 declaration is prepared and filed in 2027."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:150
msgid ""
"Before creating it, confirm the year's records are clean. The ledger "
"preflight for the annual period runs locally:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:157
msgid ""
"The rest of the annual chain resolves the four filed instalments and the "
"2026 Modelo 100 registry revision, which is published for the 2027 filing"
" season after this documentation is built, so those commands are shown as"
" display frames. `dependencies` lists each filing the declaration folds "
"in, the four Modelo 130 instalments among them, and whether its evidence "
"is satisfied. The declaration assembles itself from four kinds of source:"
" Ana's profile facts, the year's classified ledger, the four filed "
"instalments (folded in as payments on account), and any carry from an "
"earlier Renta. Employment or capital income the ledger cannot know about "
"is supplied as manual casillas, found with `bindings list --missing`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:171
msgid ""
"How every value arrives, and how to trace any figure to its rule and its "
"article of law, is the subject of [Deep dive: how the Renta declaration "
"is assembled](../explanation/how-renta-is-assembled.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:175
msgid "What you completed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/irpf-lifecycle.md:177
msgid ""
"You carried one taxpayer through a whole IRPF year: a first quarter with "
"explicit zero carries, three quarters whose carries resolved from your "
"own filed records, and an annual declaration that folded the instalments "
"into one settlement. Every figure stayed traceable to the ledger rows and"
" the rules that produced it."
msgstr ""

